      en: "The Luapula River, about 560 km long, is a major tributary of Lake Mweru in the Congo Basin. It originates in the Bangweulu swamps and flows northward, forming the border between Zambia and the DRC. Known for seasonal floods, its basin covers 115,000 km². The river supports fisheries and local transport. Potential for hydropower development exists. Its banks are densely settled, especially near Lake Mweru.",
