      en: "The Luapula Valley in northern Zambia follows the Luapula River, which drains from Lake Bangweulu to Lake Mweru. The valley is a fertile agricultural region, producing cassava, maize, and fish. The river features the Mambilima Falls, a series of rapids. Fishing is a mainstay of the local economy, providing livelihoods for the Bemba and Lunda people. The valley serves as a trade route to the DRC. Environmental issues include deforestation and mining pollution. The valley is relatively densely populated compared to surrounding areas. The climate is tropical with annual rainfall exceeding 1,200 mm.",
